/**

@page applications_exahype2_shallow_water_radial_dam_break Radial Dam Break

Here we simulate a radial dam break enclosed by a dry bathymetry ring. In the setup, a circular
dam of slightly higher water level is placed at the centre of a square domain, surrounded by
initially still water and a dry annular region. When the dam is released, a radially symmetric
wave propagates outward, interacts with the dry ring, and reflects from the boundaries.

The model is based on the two-dimensional nonlinear shallow-water equations for the water depth
\f$ h \f$, depth-averaged momenta and \f$ hu \f$, \f$ hv \f$, and the bathymetry \f$ z \f$.
The computational domain is a \f$ 10 \times 10 m^2 \f$ square. A circular dam of radius
\f$ R = 1m \f$ is centred in the middle of the domain; inside the dam the water depth is
\f$ h = 1.1m \f$, while outside the dam it is initially \f$ h = 1.0m \f$. Additionally, a dry
ring is imposed between radii \f$ 2R \f$ and \f$ 3R \f$: in this annulus the bathymetry is raised to
\f$ z = 1.2m \f$ and the water depth is set to zero, producing an initially dry region that the
wave must overtop. Everywhere else the bottom is flat with \f$ z = 0\f$.
The initial conditions are as follows:

\f{align*}{
h(x, y, 0) &= \begin{cases}
  1.1 & \text{if } r \leq{} \frac{N}{10} \\
  0.0 & \text{if } 2\frac{N}{10} \leq{} r \leq{} 3\frac{N}{10} \\
  1.0 & \text{otherwise} \\
\end{cases}, \\
hu(x, y, 0) &= 0.0, \\
hv(x, y, 0) &= 0.0, \\
b(x, y) &= \begin{cases}
  1.2 & \text{if } 2\frac{N}{10} \leq{} r \leq{} 3\frac{N}{10} \\
  0.0 & \text{otherwise} \\
\end{cases},
\f}

where @f$ (x, y) \in [0, N] \times [0, N] @f$ in meters.

*/
